  "worked_solution": "The polar curve defined by the equation $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{8}$ is the ray that starts at the origin and makes a counterclockwise angle of $\\frac{3\\pi }{8}$ with the positive $x$-axis. \n\nTherefore, the angle it makes with the negative $x$-axis is \n\n$$\n\\pi -\\frac{3\\pi }{8}=\\frac{5\\pi }{8}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe correct answer is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040587/assets/84a3340f9154465fb82fff3839a99303ead9f43462c6091ff2856e946f69746f.png)",
